<template>
    <heading>Startup code</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>startup</li>
        <li>module</li>
        <li>command</li>
        <li>dialog</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Startup is a separate phase because unit definitions precede the page elements they will use. This module runs after document parsing, when templates and mounting destinations exist, using the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/DOMContentLoaded_event"><code>DOMContentLoaded</code> event</a>. Fatal-error reporting must be installed before unit hooks run so compilation or initialization failures are visible to the user.</p>
        <p>Units opt into initialization with a synchronous <code>startup()</code> method. Hooks run in namespace property order; there is no dependency scheduler, and returned Promises are not awaited. A thrown error prevents later hooks and the initial command. A hook must finish installing what command handling needs before it returns.</p>
        <p>The initial dialog is requested through command handling so opening it also establishes which commands are legal. Displaying it directly here would bypass the operation that owns selection, loading, and eventual dialog cleanup.</p>
        <p>An unexpected failure may leave application state unreliable, so the first <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/error_event">uncaught error</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/unhandledrejection_event">unhandled rejection</a> blocks further UI use and requires a full browser reload. The first message is retained to avoid obscuring the original failure, and error text is inserted as plain text. Console diagnostics remain available. This is a barrier to user interaction, not cancellation: queued commands and async work can still run. Failures before this module installs its listeners are outside its coverage.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Startup code</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
<script type="module">
    let errorDialog;

    function showMessage(message) {
        if (errorDialog) return;
        errorDialog = document.createElement("dialog");
        errorDialog.setAttribute("role", "alertdialog");
        errorDialog.setAttribute("aria-labelledby", "LP5-FatalError-title");
        errorDialog.style.cssText = "max-width: 32rem; padding: 1.25rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere";

        const title = document.createElement("h2");
        title.id = "LP5-FatalError-title";
        title.textContent = "Execution failed";
        const detail = document.createElement("p");
        detail.textContent = message;
        detail.style.whiteSpace = "pre-wrap";
        const instruction = document.createElement("p");
        instruction.textContent = "Reload the entire page using your browser before continuing.";
        errorDialog.append(title, detail, instruction);
        errorDialog.addEventListener("cancel", event => event.preventDefault());
        document.body.append(errorDialog);
        errorDialog.showModal();
    }

    window.addEventListener("error", event => {
        showMessage(event.error?.message ?? event.message);
    });
    window.addEventListener("unhandledrejection", event => {
        showMessage(event.reason?.message ?? String(event.reason));
    });

    for (const unit of Object.values(window.LP5)) {
        if (unit && typeof unit === "object" && typeof unit.startup === "function")
            unit.startup();
    }

    window.LP5.controller.dispatch({
        name: "ModalDialog",
        dialogName: "SelectCreateProject"
    });
</script>
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
